.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt XFT_XID 3
.Os xft
.Sh NAME
.Nm xft_xid_is_start ,
.Nm xft_xid_is_continue ,
.Nm g_xid_start ,
.Nm g_xid_start_len ,
.Nm g_xid_continue ,
.Nm g_xid_continue_len
.Nd Unicode XID_Start and XID_Continue lookup and codepoint tables
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xid.h
.Ft bool
.Fn xft_xid_is_start "t_u32 cp"
.Ft bool
.Fn xft_xid_is_continue "t_u32 cp"
.Vt extern const t_u32 g_xid_start[][2];
.Vt extern const t_size g_xid_start_len;
.Vt extern const t_u32 g_xid_continue[][2];
.Vt extern const t_size g_xid_continue_len;
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn xft_xid_is_start
tests whether
.Fa cp
may start an identifier: it has the
.Ql XID_Start
property, or is
.Ql _
.Pq U+005F ,
which UAX #31 lets a profile add and which
.Ql XID_Start
itself leaves out.
.Fn xft_xid_is_continue
tests whether
.Fa cp
has the
.Ql XID_Continue
property, which already includes
.Ql _ .
Any start codepoint is also a continue codepoint.
.Pp
ASCII is answered inline through
.Xr xft_isalpha 3
and
.Xr xft_isalnum 3 ;
anything above U+007F takes a branchless binary search over the matching
table.
Values past U+10FFFF, surrogates and unassigned codepoints are never in
either set.
.Pp
.Va g_xid_start
holds the codepoints with the Unicode
.Ql XID_Start
property as
.Va g_xid_start_len
inclusive ranges, and
.Va g_xid_continue
holds the codepoints with
.Ql XID_Continue
as
.Va g_xid_continue_len
inclusive ranges.
Each entry is
.Ql {lo, hi} ;
a single codepoint is stored as
.Ql {cp, cp} .
In each table the ranges are ascending and do not overlap.
Adjacent ranges are kept as they appear in the source data and are not
merged.
.Pp
Both tables live in
.Pa src/xid/xft_xidtable.c ,
which is generated; do not edit it by hand.
.Ss Generating the tables
The tables are built from
.Pa DerivedCoreProperties.txt
of the Unicode Character Database:
.Pp
.Lk https://www.unicode.org/Public/UCD/latest/ucd/DerivedCoreProperties.txt
.Pp
The generator,
.Nm gentable ,
lives in
.Pa subprojects/gentable
and links
.Nm xft
itself, so the table is bootstrapped: the library is first built without
the xid module, then
.Nm gentable
regenerates
.Pa src/xid/xft_xidtable.c .
.Bl -enum
.It
Put
.Pa DerivedCoreProperties.txt
in the source root.
Configuring fails if it is missing.
.It
Configure and build with
.Dv XFT_BOOTSTRAP_XID
on:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cmake -S . -B build-xid -DXFT_BOOTSTRAP_XID=ON
cmake --build build-xid
.Ed
.Pp
This builds
.Pa libxft.a
without
.Pa src/xid ,
forces
.Dv XFT_BUILD_GENTABLE
on, and runs
.Nm gentable
from the source root through the
.Ql xid-table
target, which is part of the default build.
.It
Build normally; the xid module is compiled in again.
.El
.Pp
.Nm gentable
keeps only lines whose property field is
.Ql XID_Start
or
.Ql XID_Continue ;
comments and every other property are skipped.
Both are collected into one array, each entry tagged with OR'd flags: the
low bits give its shape
.Pq Dv LITERAL No or Dv RANGE
and the high bits its property
.Pq Dv START No or Dv CONTINUE ,
so an
.Ql XID_Start
range is
.Li 0x8001 .
The emitter then writes one table per property from that array.
It writes the output through a 4 KiB buffer and opens it without
.Dv O_CREAT ,
so the
.Ql xid-table
target touches the file first.
.Pp
The source data should be refetched once a year, when a new Unicode
version is published.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn xft_xid_is_start
and
.Fn xft_xid_is_continue
return
.Dv true
if
.Fa cp
is in the set and
.Dv false
otherwise.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <xft.h>

t_size	ident_len(const t_u32 *cps, t_size n)
{
	t_size	i;

	if (n == 0 || !xft_xid_is_start(cps[0]))
		return (0);
	i = 1;
	while (i < n && xft_xid_is_continue(cps[i]))
		i++;
	return (i);
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xft_ctype 3 ,
.Xr xft 7
.Sh STANDARDS
Unicode Standard Annex #31, Unicode Identifiers and Syntax.
